Disambiguate the kernel's in-tree proc-macro crates from Void's rust-std.

Void's rust-std ships proc_macro2/quote/syn in the compiler sysroot, which
upstream Rust does not. The kernel builds its own copies of these crates for
its proc-macros without excluding the sysroot, so rustc finds two candidates
for each (in-tree rlib vs. sysroot rmeta) and fails with E0464.

Drop this patch if void-packages or Rust for Linux fixes it upstream; gen.sh
will fail loudly when that happens.

--- a/template
+++ b/template
@@ -64,6 +64,17 @@
 	# avoid the strip wrapper, its used to copy the objects to a new location
 	# and required to avoid absolute relocations.
 	vsed -e "s|\$(STRIP) \(--strip-debug -o \$@ \$<;\)|/usr/bin/${STRIP} \1|" -i drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/Makefile
+
+	# Void's rust-std ships proc_macro2/quote/syn in the compiler sysroot, which
+	# upstream Rust does not. The kernel builds its own copies of these crates
+	# for its proc-macros without excluding the sysroot, so rustc finds two
+	# candidates for each (in-tree rlib vs. sysroot rmeta) and fails with E0464.
+	# Point the externs at the in-tree rlibs explicitly to disambiguate.
+	vsed -i rust/Makefile \
+		-e 's|--extern proc_macro2 \\|--extern proc_macro2=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libproc_macro2.rlib \\|g' \
+		-e 's|--extern quote \\|--extern quote=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libquote.rlib \\|g' \
+		-e 's|--extern syn \\|--extern syn=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libsyn.rlib \\|g' \
+		-e 's|--extern proc_macro2 --extern quote --extern syn|--extern proc_macro2=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libproc_macro2.rlib --extern quote=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libquote.rlib --extern syn=$(objtree)/$(obj)/libsyn.rlib|g'
 }
 
